<main class="grid-container roomy">
    <div class="grid-x grid-margin-x">
        <div class="cell large-8 medium-8 small-12">
            <h2>Meaningful Service</h2>

            <p><strong>The Community Engaged Learning (CEL) Scholars Program brings students, faculty mentors, and community partners together to learn, serve, and make a difference.</strong> Through training, mentorship, and hands-on experience, CEL Scholars work alongside communities to develop and carry out meaningful projects that address community-identified health needs.</p>

            <p>CEL Scholars explore these questions—and put what they learn into action.</p>
            <div class="indent-list">
                <ul>
                    <li>Why do some communities experience greater health challenges than others?</li>
                    <li>How do education, poverty, access to care, and other factors shape our health?</li>
                    <li><strong>What can we do together to create change?</strong></li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <p>Working with faculty mentors and more than 60 community partners, CEL Scholars listen to community priorities, develop and implement projects, and share what they learn. Along the way, they build practical skills in community engagement, project planning, evaluation, teamwork, and leadership while making a meaningful difference in the communities they serve.  Our students, faculty, staff, and community partners are guided by the <a href="https://www.texashumanities.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/108/2024/11/Code-of-Ethics.pdf?utm_source=chatgpt.com">Service-Learning Code of Ethics.</a></p>

            <p>The CEL Scholars Program prepares future health professionals to be skilled community partners and changemakers who help build healthier, more equitable communities.</p>

            <img src="https://www.texashumanities.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/108/2026/09/CEL-Scholars-Schematic-Aug-11-2026-V4.jpg" class="margin-bottom" alt="">

            <h3>Curriculum</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>ELEC 5041 - Homelessness & Addiction </li>
                <li>ELEC 5044 - Leadership in Interprofessional Community Service Learning</li>
                <li>INTD 4015 - Humanism in Medicine</li>
            </ul>

            

